# The oracle images, pinned.  One line per oracle, tab-separated: <name> <image-ref> <version line> <what it answers>.
# The image is built here (`make oracle-build`) from containers/<name>/Containerfile: the base is pinned by
# digest, the packages by exact version and SHA-256.  Two builds of one Containerfile are not two copies of one
# image, so the real guarantee is the run-time check: oracle.py compares the line `mpfr-version` prints with
# the third field, in every run, and refuses on any difference.  Raising a pin is deliberate: a new MPFR is new
# answers, and the corpus is regenerated and reviewed with it.
